  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The federal market for Other Computer Related Services, NAICS 541519, shows $14.1B in obligations for FY2026 to date, with 21,444 awards and an average award size of $656K. Obligations fell 43.4% year over year. Recent fiscal history shows higher full-year totals: FY21 $22.4B, FY22 $23.4B, FY23 $25.4B, FY24 $25.3B, and FY25 $24.9B. The FY2026 to date total is a partial figure for the fiscal year, and it is lower than the full-year totals from FY21 through FY25. Demand is concentrated among a few large buyers and vendors. The Department of Defense accounts for $3.8B in FY2026 to date obligations, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs at $1.9B and the Department of Homeland Security at $1.4B. On the vendor side, FOUR POINTS TECHNOLOGY, L.L.C. leads with $703M, THUNDERCAT TECHNOLOGY, LLC follows with $667M, and V3GATE, LLC is third with $585M. These figures describe the current size, recent trend, and concentration of the market through FY2026 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal spending trended in NAICS 541519 since FY2021?",
        "body": "Obligations rose from FY21 $22.4B to a peak of FY23 $25.4B, then held near that level in FY24 $25.3B and FY25 $24.9B. FY2026 to date obligations are $14.1B, which is a partial fiscal-year total and is down 43.4% year over year. The average award size for FY2026 to date is $656K across 21,444 awards. That combination shows a lower fiscal-year-to-date total compared with the prior full years."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and contractors dominate NAICS 541519 spending in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense leads federal buying with $3.8B in obligations, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $1.9B and the Department of Homeland Security with $1.4B. Other major buyers include the Department of Health and Human Services at $1.2B and the Department of the Treasury at $914M. Vendor concentration is also visible: FOUR POINTS TECHNOLOGY, L.L.C. has $703M, THUNDERCAT TECHNOLOGY, LLC has $667M, and V3GATE, LLC has $585M in FY2026 to date obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
